                <pb facs="0911" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/587: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-15T18:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 17,
                            4.36 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Last night and today over 30 people have been arrested and imprisoned and some of
                    them badly injured by the policemen. For the first time the Tinoco agents have
                    broken into houses to capture men. List includes three brothers of ex-President
                    Gonzalez, brothers of ex-Minister for Foreign Affairs Julio Acosta, prominent
                    lawyers, and others. Recruits are being made, and more talk of invasion. A
                    friend of Federico Tinoco, Dr. Uribe, said today that encouragement had been
                    received from the President of Guatemala to fight to very last because he said
                    that the attitude of Washington was a bluff. Other desperadoes are reported to
                    have left here to reach the United States to kill Alfredo Gonzalez. They must
                    get the visé in some other country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
